From: Ian Blenke <ian@blenke.com>
Date: Thu, 4 Jun 2026 09:48:31 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 00446/11171] [conductor] In-process docs for FR-11 continuous
 self-learning v20 -- APPLY the Tier-3 predictor as a fast-path/early-exit
 cascade gate (distinct from v19's TRAINING of it): wire the trained
 FR11ExtendedJEPA predictor (exp3788, predictive AUROC 0.9715) so that when it
 is CONFIDENT, the pipeline FAST-PATH-SKIPS the full 4-verifier ensemble
 scoring, and only falls through to full scoring when the predictor is
 uncertain. Measure the COMPUTE SAVING (fraction of candidates
 short-circuited) AND confirm NO accuracy regression vs full scoring on a
 held-out FoVer split (the frozen 0.9131 effective AUROC is preserved at the
 chosen confidence threshold). The Partial-Reward-Model early-rejection
 pattern (arXiv:2508.01969). CPU; the mandated self-learning experiment.

Co-Authored-By: Gemini CLI <noreply@google.com>
