@@ -8595,3 +8595,4 @@ Did NOT modify research-roadmap.yaml or scripts/research_conductor.py. Did NOT p
 - 2026-06-04: HARDEN the banked product: MITIGATE the context_compaction gaming evasion. .347 exp3790 found the shipped 4-verifier ensemble DEGRADES under the context_compaction perturbation (true-but-irrelevant padding that hides the wrong step). Implement a targeted, CPU-only mitigation (e.g. a compaction-robust feature / normalization in the scoring path) and RE-MEASURE the gaming-degradation curve to show whether the evasion is closed (or quantify how much it narrows) -- WITHOUT regressing clean-corpus AUROC (the frozen 0.9131 ensemble behavior on un-perturbed FoVer must be preserved). CPU, cached triples -- NO live LLM, NO GPU, NOT a moat reopen. Reports a before/after curve; makes NO new headline claim. (✅ Complete) — honest_verdict=complete: gaming_resistance_mitigation_v2_context_compaction_closed_clean_auroc_preserved_n240_not_a_moat_reopen_headline_unchanged; results/experiment_3800_gaming_resistance_mitigation_v2.json
 - 2026-06-04: HARDEN the banked product: add the THIRD integration surface (HTTP/REST) for the certified abstention mode. .346 wired it into the verify API; .347 added the CLI+batch surface; this adds a minimal HTTP/REST endpoint (POST a candidate -> confident-or-abstain verdict + the certified coverage/risk/delta metadata) so a non-Python integrator can call abstention-gated verification over the network (Decentralization Rule 4). Edits CODE + tests only; default abstention OFF; emits a doc-update PROPOSAL for the operator-curated docs (does NOT edit them). No accuracy claim -- a wiring smoke. (⚠️ Blocked) — honest_verdict=blocked_http_abstention_e2e_failed; results/experiment_3801_abstention_http_rest_surface.json
 - 2026-06-04: REPAIR the endorsed process tool: TUNE the Anomaly-Escalation classifier (scripts/anomaly_escalation_classifier.py). .347 exp3791 validated it and found false-escalation rate 0.83 (it escalates 83% of CLEAN bounded negatives) with frame-violating recall 1.0 -> supports_wiring_in=false. Tune the classification rules to drive false-escalation DOWN to a usable level (target <=0.2) WITHOUT dropping frame-violating recall below 1.0, then RE-VALIDATE against the same historical corpus and report the new confusion matrix. The classifier MUST still only ever recommend pause+escalate, never relax verification. Recommend-only; conductor unmodified. (✅ Complete) — honest_verdict=complete: anomaly_escalation_v2_tuned_false_escalation_0.833333_to_0.000000_frame_violating_recall_1.0_never_relaxes_verification_supports_wiring_in_true_conductor_unmodified; results/experiment_3802_anomaly_escalation_classifier_v2_tuning.json
